# Photograph the game's own Zeal indicator on both sides of TWO melee blows
# thrown by the paladin who holds the spell: one at the target the spell chose,
# one at a second creature. This is the session for bd inc-tek.31.
#
#   tools/headless.sh tools/keys/zeal-strike.keys 4
#
# Read the result with tools/check_zeal_strike.sh, which is what asserts. This
# file only produces the screens.
#
# WHAT THE BEAD CLAIMS. lib/pspells.irh's Zeal is a copy of Sanctuary and
# carries Sanctuary's defect unchanged. It registers three TRAP_EVENT stati on
# landing -- EVICTIM(EV_STRIKE), EV_EFFECT and EV_MAGIC_STRIKE -- but defines
# handlers for EVICTIM(EV_STRIKE), EV_STRIKE and EV_MAGIC_STRIKE. The two lists
# do not match. Event dispatch (src/Event.cpp:322-340) calls a trap's effect
# only when META(S->Mag) equals the event being thrown, so META(EV_STRIKE) --
# the handler that ends the spell when the paladin attacks somebody other than
# his chosen target -- is unreachable. The spell's own Desc promises "If the
# paladin attacks any other target, the effect ceases -- the target is free to
# attack him in turn."
#
# WHY THIS SESSION NEEDS TWO BLOWS AND NOT ONE. Zeal is not a plain copy of
# Sanctuary: it adds an exemption so that the paladin may strike his chosen
# target and keep the spell. All three handlers open with the same test,
#
#   if (GetHandle(EVictim) == EActor->GetEffStatiObj(EFF_FLAG1,$"Zeal"))
#     return NOTHING;
#
# against a flag granted at cast time as $"zeal". A check that measured only
# "Zeal ends on a blow" would pass a build in which that exemption had been
# broken, which is the exact opposite of what the spell is for. So the session
# strikes the CHOSEN target first and then the OTHER one, and the two readings
# have to disagree.
#
# THE ORACLE IS THE STATUS LINE. src/Term.cpp:185 walks the player's stati on
# every redraw and prints the name of any T_TEFFECT stati whose effect carries
# EF_SHOWNAME. Zeal carries it, so the bottom line of the map screen reads
#
#   HP:31/31 Mana:19/19 FP:4/4 GP:11           Zeal Globe of Shadow |
#
# for exactly as long as the paladin holds the spell, and stops the moment the
# stati goes. The key script cannot write that word: it only sends keystrokes,
# and the string comes from the player's live stati list, not from a message
# that could linger in the message window. ("Globe of Shadow" beside it is the
# babau's own darkness, not part of the measurement.)
#
# FIVE PHOTOGRAPHS, and the comparisons between them are the whole test:
#
#   after-cast       the spell has just landed -- Zeal MUST be shown
#   after-nonattack  three searches later -- MUST still be shown
#   after-chosen     one blow at the CHOSEN target later -- MUST still be shown
#   after-other      one blow at the SECOND babau later -- MUST be gone
#
# THE FIRST TWO ARE CONTROLS AND THEY ARE NOT DECORATION. Without them a build
# that never applied Zeal at all, or one that dropped it on any turn that
# passed, would show an absent indicator after the second blow and would be
# read as proof that the blow ended it. The searches spend real game time
# (measured on seed 4: turn 198021 at after-cast, 198030 at after-nonattack).
#
# WIZARD MODE SUPPLIES THE SPELL AND BOTH TARGETS, because no scripted walk
# can be relied on to find any of them.
#
#   * Freeze Monsters (the eleventh row of the Wizard Mode Switches list) stops
#     the babaus acting. A babau that fought back would attack the player,
#     which is EVICTIM(EV_STRIKE) -- a different handler, and one that rolls a
#     saving throw. This session must measure the paladin's own blows only.
#   * "Learn Any Spell" takes a typed name and sets SP_KNOWN|SP_PRIMAL|SP_INNATE
#     (src/Debug.cpp:862). An innate spell costs no mana, so the character
#     reaches the blows with the spell up whatever the seed gave him. A quoted
#     string in a key script is sent one character per keystroke, which is how
#     "Zeal" reaches the ReadLine.
#   * A babau, and not the goblin that tools/keys/sanctuary-strike.keys uses,
#     for two reasons. Zeal's EV_ISTARGET returns CANNOT_CAST_IT unless the
#     victim isMType(MA_EVIL), and a babau is always Chaotic Evil. And the
#     chosen target has to survive being hit, because the session goes on to
#     strike the other creature afterwards: a babau has 7d20+35 hit points
#     against a first-level paladin's 1d8+1 +2d6-vs-evil, and a goblin would
#     not have lived through the first blow.
#   * The paladin's sacred mount stands immediately WEST of him on arrival, so
#     the two babaus go EAST (the chosen target) and NORTH (the other one).
#     Striking west would hit his own horse.
#
# @choose "Zeal" presses the Spell Manager letter beside the spell, which casts
# it outright -- ENTER afterwards would be a second, separate command. The
# RIGHT then ENTER after it answer the spell's own Q_TAR prompt: RIGHT walks
# the target cursor one square east onto the chosen babau, ENTER takes it.
#
# The player-data dump is corroboration, not the oracle: wizard mode "Examine
# Player Data" prints every stati with its event code, so the three TRAP EVENT
# rows tagged (eID:Zeal) show which events the spell actually trapped. On the
# unfixed build their Mag values are 2019, 52 and 83 -- EVICTIM(EV_STRIKE),
# EV_EFFECT and EV_MAGIC_STRIKE; the fix turns the 52 into a 19. It is
# scrolled to with DOWN because the dump is longer than the screen.

@include chargen-paladin.keys

# Freeze Monsters, the eleventh row of the switches list.
w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*10
SPACE
ESC

w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Zeal"
ENTER

# The chosen target, east of the player.
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Demons"
@choose "babau"
RIGHT
ENTER

# The other creature, north of the player.
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Demons"
@choose "babau"
UP
ENTER

m
@choose "Zeal"
RIGHT
ENTER
@dump:after-cast

# What the traps actually are, before anything disturbs them.
w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
DOWN*40
@dump:traps-before
ESC

# --- the first control: three searches, none of them an attack -------------
s
s
s
@dump:after-nonattack

# --- the blow at the CHOSEN target: Zeal must survive it -------------------
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
@dump:after-chosen
v
@dump:chosen-log
@while "Messages" ESC

# --- the blow at the OTHER creature: Zeal must end --------------------------
UP
@while "Confirm attack" y
@dump:after-other
v
@dump:other-log
@while "Messages" ESC

w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
DOWN*40
@dump:traps-after
ESC
@quit
